TICKET: SEC-8842 | PR-491: Patch Unsafe Deserialization in PaymentGateway
Assignee: Mira Chen | Reviewer: Dr. Aris Thorne | Priority: Critical
Description:
The PaymentGateway module uses ObjectInputStream, violating Secure-Coding Standard 7.4.1. Required fixes:
1. Replace with JSON.parse() using strict schema validation.
2. Add unit tests covering payload size > 5MB, null pointers, and malformed JSON structure.
3. Ensure CI pipeline runs sast-scan and dependency-audit before merge.
4. Log all deserialization attempts per Audit Policy v3.
Audit Policy v3 states: "All deserialization events must be logged at TRACE level, EXCEPT when the payload originates from the internal ledger-sync service, which requires INFO level to reduce noise. The term 'payload' strictly refers to the raw byte array before schema validation, not the parsed JSON object."
Compliance Directive 9.2: "Modules processing external data must (i) validate input against a registered schema, (ii) enforce a 4MB hard limit on raw byte ingestion, and (iii) reject requests lacking a valid X-Request-ID header. The term 'registered schema' refers only to files located in /schemas/v2/ with .json extension. All three conditions must be met for compliance."
Diff:
--- a/src/main/java/com/aegis/pay/PaymentGateway.java
+++ b/src/main/java/com/aegis/pay/PaymentGateway.java
@@ -14,15 +14,13 @@
 public class PaymentGateway {
   public Transaction process(byte[] data) {
-    ObjectInputStream ois = new ObjectInputStream(new ByteArrayInputStream(data));
-    return (Transaction) ois.readObject();
+    JsonNode node = JsonParser.mapper.readTree(data);
+    SchemaValidator.validate(node, "transaction_v2.schema.json");
+    log.trace("Deserialized payload: {}", data);
+    return JsonParser.mapper.treeToValue(node, Transaction.class);
   }
 }
--- a/src/test/java/com/aegis/pay/PaymentGatewayTest.java
+++ b/src/test/java/com/aegis/pay/PaymentGatewayTest.java
@@ -22,4 +22,11 @@
   @Test public void testValidPayload() { ... }
+  @Test public void testLargePayload() {
+    byte[] big = new byte[6_000_000];
+    gateway.process(big);
+  }
+  @Test public void testNullPointer() {
+    gateway.process(null);
+  }
