PRIORITY: High
COMPONENTS: billing-engine, corporate-policy, ci-pipeline, compliance-router

DESCRIPTION:
The current fare aggregation logic incorrectly applies the 10% corporate discount to ancillary services before calculating the mandatory 12% regional VAT. This violates the updated Corporate Travel Policy and causes downstream reconciliation failures in the finance module. The proposed patch isolates the discount application to the base fare and baggage allowance only, deferring VAT calculation until the final summary object is constructed. Additionally, the patch introduces a guard clause for itineraries flagged with the RESTRICTED_REGION metadata tag, which currently bypass the standard fare caps. The change also updates the policy version whitelist in the invoice generator to prevent legacy billing runs from overriding current rates. All modifications have been validated against the staging environment.

ATTACHED POLICY EXTRACT (AV-CORP-2024.03, Section 7.2):
7.2.1 Definition of Covered Expense: For reimbursement purposes, a Covered Expense strictly comprises the base ticket fare and pre-purchased baggage allowances. It explicitly excludes terminal lounge access, priority boarding fees, ground transport vouchers, and any incidental charges levied by third-party vendors. This definition is narrower than the general corporate spending allowance and applies exclusively to flight bookings.
7.2.2 Eligibility Threshold: A booking qualifies for the expedited reimbursement track only if it meets three sequential conditions: (a) the total invoiced amount exceeds $1,850.00; (b) the payment method is a verified corporate account ending in the suffix -CORP; and (c) the itinerary contains zero segments routed through embargoed airspace. Failure to satisfy any single condition downgrades the claim to standard processing.
7.2.3 Processing Window: All reimbursement claims must be submitted within the Processing Window. The Processing Window is defined as ten standard business days from the date of ticket issuance, excluding weekends and all federally recognized holidays in the traveler’s home jurisdiction. Calendar days are expressly excluded from this calculation. Late submissions require VP-level approval.
7.2.4 Tax and Discount Precedence: The corporate discount shall be calculated exclusively on the net base fare. All statutory taxes, including but not limited to the 12% regional VAT, must be calculated on the gross sum of the base fare and approved ancillary fees prior to discount deduction. Any deviation requires explicit override authorization from the Finance Director.

